.TH LIMINE-VFIO 1 "September 2026" "limine-vfio 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
limine-vfio \- dynamic PCI device passthrough manager for the Limine bootloader
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B limine-vfio
\fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGUMENTS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B limine-vfio
is an automated, device-agnostic VFIO passthrough and hardware isolation management utility designed for Arch Linux and CachyOS systems utilizing the
.B Limine
bootloader.
.PP
It automates PCI device discovery, automatic hardware classification, IOMMU group isolation checks, modular profile management, dynamic Limine boot entry generation, host driver exclusion, and libvirt XML snippet generation.
.PP
Supported hardware categories include Graphics Processing Units (GPUs), Network Interface Cards (NICs), PCIe USB controllers, NVMe/SATA storage controllers, Audio controllers, Video capture cards, and Hardware Accelerators (TPUs, NPUs, FPGAs).

.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B check
Performs pre-flight system checks, verifying CPU virtualization (AMD-V / Intel VT-x), IOMMU kernel status, initramfs module configuration (/etc/mkinitcpio.conf), Limine bootloader tools, and post-hook deployment.
.TP
.B list-devices \fR(aliases: \fBlist\fR, \fBdevices\fR)
Displays a colorized table of all detected PCI devices, their classifications (GPU, NETWORK, USB, STORAGE, CAPTURE, ACCELERATOR, AUDIO, SYSTEM), vendor/device PCI IDs, active driver bindings, and IOMMU group mappings.
.TP
.B status
Displays current kernel command-line parameters, active \fBvfio-pci\fR driver bindings in the running session, and all configured profiles in \fI/etc/vfio-passthrough.d/\fR.
.TP
.B add
Runs an interactive wizard guiding the user through device selection, companion function pairing (e.g. HDMI audio controllers on GPUs), IOMMU group isolation verification, drop-in profile creation in \fI/etc/vfio-passthrough.d/<profile>.conf\fR, kernel command-line registration in \fI/etc/default/limine\fR, secondary NVIDIA driver exclusion, and bootloader menu regeneration via \fBlimine-update\fR.
.TP
.B remove \fR[\fIPROFILE\fR]
Interactively or by argument removes a configured profile, cleans up corresponding entries from \fI/etc/default/limine\fR, and triggers \fBlimine-update\fR.
.TP
.B generate-xml \fR[\fIPROFILE\fR | \fIPCI_ADDRESS\fR] \fR(aliases: \fBxml\fR, \fBvirt-xml\fR)
Outputs formatted libvirt \fB<hostdev>\fR XML blocks for the specified profile or PCI device (e.g., \fI82:00.0\fR). Output is ready to paste directly into \fBvirt-manager\fR or \fBvirsh edit\fR.
.TP
.B doctor \fR(aliases: \fBfix\fR, \fBconflicts\fR)
Scans for bootloader and configuration conflicts (such as orphan Limine entries, missing kernel parameters for enabled profiles, or accidental isolation of the primary host display GPU) and provides interactive, automated conflict resolution and bootloader synchronization.
.TP
.B install \fR(aliases: \fBsetup\fR)
Manual installation routine deploying the post-hook to \fI/etc/boot/hooks/post.d/95-vfio-entries\fR, initializing configuration directories, and creating binary symlinks. (Used when not installing via Arch package manager).
.TP
.B help \fR(aliases: \fB--help\fR, \fB-h\fR)
Displays command-line usage and available subcommands.

.SH CONFIGURATION FILES
.TP
.I /etc/vfio-passthrough.d/*.conf
Drop-in device configuration files. Each file defines:
.RS
.B PROFILE
- Unique profile identifier.
.br
.B DEVICE_TYPE
- Device category (GPU, NETWORK, USB, STORAGE, etc.).
.br
.B DESCRIPTION
- Human-readable description.
.br
.B PCI_IDS
- Comma-separated list of vendor:device IDs to bind to \fBvfio-pci\fR.
.br
.B ENABLED
- Enable/disable toggle (\fIyes\fR / \fIno\fR).
.RE
.TP
.I /etc/vfio-passthrough.conf
Global configuration defining system-wide IOMMU kernel parameters (\fIIOMMU_PARAMS\fR). If omitted, CPU vendor parameters are auto-detected.
.TP
.I /etc/boot/hooks/post.d/95-vfio-entries
Dynamic Limine post-hook script executed by \fBlimine-update\fR to generate kernel passthrough boot entries.

.SH SAFEGUARDS
The utility checks for:
.IP \(bu 2
UEFI boot mode (\fI/sys/firmware/efi\fR).
.IP \(bu 2
Hardware CPU virtualization flags (\fIvmx\fR or \fIsvm\fR in \fI/proc/cpuinfo\fR).
.IP \(bu 2
Active Limine configuration (\fI/boot/limine.conf\fR).
.IP \(bu 2
IOMMU grouping isolation to warn against isolating devices that share groups with critical host controllers.

.SH EXAMPLES
.B limine-vfio check
.RS
Verify system readiness for VFIO passthrough.
.RE
.PP
.B limine-vfio list-devices
.RS
List and classify all PCI devices with their IOMMU groups.
.RE
.PP
.B sudo limine-vfio add
.RS
Launch interactive configuration wizard.
.RE
.PP
.B limine-vfio generate-xml 1060
.RS
Output libvirt hostdev XML for the '1060' profile.
.RE

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lspci (8),
.BR virsh (1),
.BR mkinitcpio (8)

